{
 "_doc": "Tier-2 wilderness dungeon (forest site, random worlds): a backcountry ranger district station the Cordon made a checkpoint on the forest road, with a 15 m steel fire-weather tower in its chain-link compound. The tower is four stacked lattice sections (w4_ranger_tower_leg_section, level 0 with y) round a recorder hut (L0) and three 2 x 2 landings (L1-L3, open edges with rails), climbed by four real ladders through hatches into the steel-clad cab (L4, the w4_ranger_tower_cab shell). Route: the road ends at the barrier -> the screening shelter (entering it, or opening the booth door, wakes the held families: ambush) -> the booth and the Cordon's roster -> through the open gate -> the office door (can chime) -> the office and the district log -> the radio room: the weather log and the tower key -> the bunkhouse (opening its door or the loose boards wake the crew: ambush) -> the engine bay past the brush truck (jaws by the back door) -> draw the bolt on the bay's back door (the shortcut) -> the weather yard -> unlock the recorder hut -> four ladders up the tower -> the cab: the radio, the district key, the district ranger (guardian) -> back down, and the district key opens the gun safe in the office. Hollowed don't climb ladders: once the cab is cleared the tower is a refuge. See docs/POI_AUTHORING.md.",
